diff --git a/docs/dev/config/services.md b/docs/dev/config/services.md
index 62782c6..63ce1b7 100644
--- a/docs/dev/config/services.md
+++ b/docs/dev/config/services.md
@@ -3,7 +3,7 @@
 
 This document describes the device data model parameters one should consider when creating a network services configuration template. For a wider picture, please see [](dev-device-features) or [](../devices.md).
 
-The services module currently supports two client-server services: **DNS** (fully implemented) and **syslog** (attribute schema defined, transformation logic ready, configuration templates not yet implemented).
+This fork adds a third: **SNMP** (agent only, implemented as a SERVER -- see the SNMP note in the user documentation). Upstream, the services module currently supports two client-server services: **DNS** (fully implemented) and **syslog** (attribute schema defined, transformation logic ready, configuration templates not yet implemented).
 
 **Notes:**
 
