--- a/docs/module/services.md
+++ b/docs/module/services.md
@@ -3,6 +3,8 @@
 
 The Network Services configuration module implements DNS and Syslog clients and servers; NTP and SNMP are planned for future releases.
 
+This *netlab* fork also implements an **SNMP agent** (`services.server.snmp`) -- see [SNMP agent](#services-snmp) below.
+
 ```eval_rst
 .. contents:: Table of Contents
    :depth: 2
@@ -70,3 +72,61 @@ The DNS server is enabled on supported nodes with the **services.server.dns** pa
 
 * Specify the Syslog server(s) on client nodes with the [common network services parameters](services-common-parameters)
 * The syslog server is enabled on supported nodes with the **services.server.syslog: True** parameter.
+
+(services-snmp)=
+## SNMP agent
+
+```{note}
+SNMP is a **Skyforge extension**. Upstream *netlab* lists SNMP as planned for a
+future release; this fork implements the agent half now. Changes belong in
+`patches/netlab/`.
+```
+
+An SNMP agent is modelled as a **server**, not a client: it listens on UDP/161 and
+answers an NMS, exactly as a DNS server answers a resolver. It is therefore
+configured under `services.server.snmp`, and is deliberately absent from the
+module's `clients` list -- a node that only needs an `snmp-server community` line
+has no server to point at, and modelling it as a client would fail validation with
+*"is neither a client nor a server"*.
+
+Trap and inform *destinations* are the genuine client half of SNMP. They are not
+implemented yet and would arrive as `services.snmp.server` without disturbing this.
+
+| Operating system | SNMP agent |
+| ---------------- | :--: |
+| Arista EOS | ✅ |
+| Cisco IOS / IOS-XE | ✅ |
+
+Devices inheriting from `ios` (`iol`, `iosv`, `csr`, `cat8000v`, …) inherit the
+capability.
+
+### Parameters
+
+* `services.server.snmp.community` -- read-only community string. Defaults to `skyforge` (the community the collector's collectors poll with).
+* `services.server.snmp.location` -- optional `snmp-server location`.
+* `services.server.snmp.contact` -- optional `snmp-server contact`.
+
+Setting `services.server.snmp: True` enables the agent with the default community.
+
+### Example
+
+```yaml
+module: [ services ]
+
+nodes:
+  s1:
+    device: eos
+    services.server.snmp:
+      community: skyforge
+      location: lab-a
+```
+
+renders
+
+```
+snmp-server community skyforge ro
+snmp-server location lab-a
+```
+
+The access level is spelled per platform -- `ro` on EOS, `RO` on IOS -- because
+these strings are written to the device verbatim.
diff --git a/netsim/ansible/templates/services/arubacx.j2 b/netsim/ansible/templates/services/arubacx.j2
